---
// The Restore line (glossary "Restore"; ticket 10 § Returning visitor: resume): a
// returning visitor's single line, shown only while the shell mounts, no floor
// (contrast `BootScreen`'s 600 ms floor / 1.5 s ceiling — there is none here).
// Same ground as `BootScreen` (full-viewport black, CRT classes), shown by
// `shell.css` only while `html.restore` is set, and hidden again once
// `html.shell-ready` says the island has taken over. `aria-hidden` throughout
// (ticket 14 § Boot and resume): the desktop-ready status is a single announcement
// from the island, not from this screen.
//
// `#restore-line` starts with the zero-windows wording so that a skip mid-*first*
// boot (ticket 10 § Skip: "the island has not mounted yet ... never a blank
// screen") — which shows this element without ever having gone through
// `HeadGate`'s restore branch — still reads as a sensible line rather than empty
// text. `HeadGate.astro`'s script overwrites this text on an actual restore.
---

<div id="restore" class="scan" aria-hidden="true">
  <p id="restore-line" class="bloom">
    RESUME &middot; DESKTOP RESTORED
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  #restore {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 2;
    background: #000;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    /* Slashed zero (ticket 13): chrome/log output, not body copy. */
    font-feature-settings: 'zero';
  }

  #restore-line {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
